      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the reason for the existence of these factory methods is that the role is a mandatory parameter, then it\u0027s probably better to do that by making the role a mandatory parameter in the constructor. Remember to add @IntDef for it.\n\nPresumably it needs to be possible for someone to pass in ROLE_ANY - or at least, it seems like a useful thing to do, for example, if some app wants to register a callback for any L2CAP network regardless of whether it\u0027s server or client?\n\nOr maybe this isn\u0027t actually mandatory, and we can just say that the default is ANY, and if the caller wants another role then they can do setRole?\n\nIt think the same considerations actually probably apply for compression.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 253,
        "startChar": 76,
        "endLine": 253,
        "endChar": 90
