      "writtenOn": "2024-12-24T04:27:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Presumably there needs to be a guard value that indicates the lack of a PSM? Maybe -1 or 0? That probably needs to be a public constant (PSM_ANY?) that is in the API surface.\n\nConsider whether there need to be separate values for \"any PSM\" and \"no PSM\". More specifically, do you need both a \"no PSM\" value that matches any PSMs and a \"no PSM\" value that doesn\u0027t match any PSM?\n\nIt sounds like because the specifier contains a role, we don\u0027t actually need two separate values here, and we just need a PSM_ANY.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 147,
        "startChar": 54,
        "endLine": 147,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "deb354fbd2a7f60194755f7d83fb4dd76b9b5efa",
